# Environment for the Playwright suite. Loaded by `vite dev --mode test`.
#
# This file exists because of a precedence trap. `playwright.config.ts` used to
# pass the value inline:
#
#   PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3010 npx vite dev --port 3010
#
# which works in CI and silently does not work locally. CI has no `.env`, so the
# shell variable is the only source. Locally Vite loads `.env` into the SSR
# worker's process.env and the shell value is lost, so the app falls back to the
# default in src/server/env.ts — `http://localhost:4321`, the *dev* port.
#
# The recovery email is then minted with a redirect to :4321 while the test
# browser is on :3010. The PKCE verifier cookie lives on the origin that
# requested the reset, so the exchange fails on the other origin and the user
# lands on /login. The symptom is a password-reset test failing with "element
# not found" for a heading — nothing that points at env precedence.
#
# `.env.[mode]` beats `.env`, so putting it here makes the suite behave the same
# way whether or not a developer has a `.env`. Committed deliberately: it holds
# no secrets, only which port the tests run on.
PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3010
